The Stranger, whose name is Vesper Feep, is an entity trapped at the center of [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]]. [[Org/Althane/The Weft|The Weft]] have long called him the Feep. He came from [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Terminus|Terminus]], the great city on [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]], where he was a media mogul before he became what he is. He is remembered as the one who stole the shard of nothing from the nothing before him.

He was born poor in Terminus: a hungry orphan with a rough red lens set into his ruined left eye, stealing food off a street cart. He ran with a pack of ragged children and led them, and an older man with gold set into his face, pleased with the boy's acting, took him on. He rose in that man's company; when the man told him there was no room for him above, Vesper pushed him from a high terrace. He came to make a talk show called the Spotlight, built like the Lighthouse with the same three-part band and the same guest chair, and in time he sat on the board of [[Org/Omnivox/index|Omnivox]]. When the board moved to remove him, armed men came into the boardroom, and he chose to stay.

He holds the [[Phenomena/Echo Fragment|Echo Fragment]], which he took from its previous holder, [[People/Althane/Karen Sill|Karen Sill]], who was brought to him sedated and bound. When he took it, the whole of his life was torn out of every record, save for what stands three times removed from him, which might yet be found. What power he has is not his own: it comes from the fragment, or from divine beings he has taken in, and he is no caster. He ascended, went to take the power he saw, and the Lighthouse caught him almost at once.

He has no body of his own, only a presence spread through the air above the drop at the center of Althane. Bound to the local weave by a [[Phenomena/Althane/Godpiercer|godpiercer]] driven into the densest part of him, he has been drawn into a single mortal body: an angry man who still carries the fragment's power. At his side he keeps an accompaniment, a band of three musicians puppeted by runes that stand out of their limbs and torso, and they play as the band of the Spotlight played.

The route he took out of Syrin left a trail of broken space in the planet's orbit, which [[People/Althane/The Broker|the Broker]] follows to find where he came from. That trail narrows his point of departure to the station that stands over Syrin as [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Gilded Spire/index|the Gilded Spire]].

Tech of Sedecium holds that the Feep is as he is because he was already so, and that taking the fragment from him, or leaving it, will change nothing in the world. Its true name survives only in the records of Omnivox on Syrin, and Tech holds that to learn it would make the Stranger vulnerable.
